{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HEB",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us therefore fear, lest a promise being left ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of entering into his rest, any of you should seem to come short of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For to us was the gospel preached, as well as to them: but the word which they heard did not profit them, not being mixed with faith in them that heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we who have believed do enter into rest, as he said, As I have sworn in my wrath, if they shall enter into my rest: although the works were finished from the foundation of the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he spoke in a certain place of the seventh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on this wise, And God rested the seventh day from all his works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " again, If they shall enter into my rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing therefore it remaineth that some must enter into it, and they to whom it was first preached entered not because of unbelief:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Again, he limiteth a certain day, saying in David, To-day, after so long a time; as it is said, To-day, if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if Jesus had given them rest, then he would not afterward have spoken of another day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he that hath entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works, as God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "did",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from his.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us labor therefore to enter into that rest, lest any man fall after the same example of unbelief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the word of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " living, and powerful, and sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit, and of the joints and marrow, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither is there any creature that is not manifest in his sight: but all things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " naked and opened to the eyes of him with whom we have to do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing then that we have a great High Priest, that hath passed into the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold fast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " profession.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we have not a high priest who cannot be touched with the feeling of our infirmities; but who was in all points tempted as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "we are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us therefore come boldly to the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
